+## MFG Unlocker
+
+On an RTX 30-series card, DLSS frame generation can also be unlocked
+with the released MFG Unlocker DLL (dashdogy/MFG-Unlocker v1.7.2, MIT),
+instead of FSR 3. Run `.\Get-MFG.cmd` once: it fetches the author's
+release (about 5 MB) into `mfg\` (git-ignored) and checks its SHA-256.
+Then start with `-Mfg` (or `victory play --mfg`); the F1 menu's FRAME
+GENERATION item then switches it 2X to 6X while playing, as on an
+RTX 40/50 card.
+
+The DLL is the author's own release, fetched by the user; this
+repository does not carry it, the same as NVIDIA's and AMD's files.
+It is loaded before Streamline and patches the DLSS-G provider in
+memory only — the provider's Ada minimum (0x190) becomes Ampere
+(0x170) and its >2x count gate is lifted — so Streamline reports
+frame generation as supported. No file, driver or Streamline code
+is changed. It is never used together with FSR 3 frame generation:
+DLSS wins if both are asked for.
+
+2x is the likely win; 3x to 6x depends on the count-gate patch
+landing for the exact DLSS-G provider Streamline 2.14.16 ships. The
+Unlocker's own log (`RTXMFG-*.log` beside `victory.exe`) says which
+provider it saw and what it patched. And it only shows more frames
+per rendered frame — it does not render faster, so the rendered rate
+stays where it was. Its Backspace menu may not appear in this title
+(it hooks the present for its overlay); the unlock does not need it.
+
